# NES: a game that scribbles its battery RAM continuously (work RAM, like Zelda
# 1) is still saved, and keeps being saved: the first dump follows the first
# write, and the core's next notice (it re-announces as soon as a dump clears
# its flag) earns a second dump a few seconds later.
expect-screen "TangCore"
press b
expect-screen "game.nes"
press down
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-core nestang
churn on
wram-burst 0x000 512 0xA5
expect-file saves/nes/game.sav size 8192
wait-dump 12s
churn off
